From 51e1398e77e3b677799b1ef0f3da236f8a7be0b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:38:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] media: v4l2-jpeg: fix the end of DHT segment parsing
To: Mauro Carvalho Chehab <mchehab@kernel.org>
Cc: Hans Verkuil <hverkuil@kernel.org>,
    Philipp Zabel <p.zabel@pengutronix.de>,
    Mirela Rabulea <mirela.rabulea@nxp.com>,
    imx@lists.linux.dev,
    linux-media@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

jpeg_parse_huffman_tables() subtracts the two length bytes from len
before its loop, but ends with jpeg_skip(stream, len - 2). For every
well-formed DHT segment len is 0 there, so it asks to skip -2 bytes.
The size_t wraps, stream->curr + len wraps to two bytes before the
current position, the bounds check passes, and parsing resumes on the
last two HUFFVAL bytes. Valid baseline tables never hold 0xff there, so
this goes unnoticed, but a table that ends in ff db makes the parser
take a DQT marker that is not there.

A table whose BITS count more symbols than the segment holds is not
rejected either: HUFFVAL is read from the following segments and the
loop leaves len negative, which again turns into a backwards skip, so
the bogus table can be accepted.

Reject tables that overrun their segment and skip the remainder of the
segment with the right length.

Fixes: 50733b5b9102 ("media: add v4l2 JPEG helpers")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c
index 36a0f1a1b..958d64d89 100644
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-jpeg.c
@@ -514,6 +514,9 @@ static int jpeg_parse_huffman_tables(struct jpeg_stream *stream,
 
 			mt += li;
 		}
+		/* Tc/Th, BITS and HUFFVAL must fit in the segment */
+		if (17 + mt > len)
+			return -EINVAL;
 		/* HUFFVAL - values associated with each Huffman code */
 		ret = jpeg_skip(stream, mt);
 		if (ret < 0)
@@ -525,7 +528,8 @@ static int jpeg_parse_huffman_tables(struct jpeg_stream *stream,
 		}
 	}
 
-	return jpeg_skip(stream, len - 2);
+	/* len no longer includes the length field itself. */
+	return jpeg_skip(stream, len);
 }
 
 /* B.2.4.4 Restart interval definition syntax */
